{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474045-the-shen-purview-and-motif-how-do-they-work-together","id":1474045,"title":"The Shen purview and motif - how do they work together?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-05T11:16:41-08:00","id":1474045,"title":"The Shen purview and motif - how do they work together?","content":"The Shen purview is Tianming - power over bureaucracies, mortal and celestial. Cutting aside mortal red tape with your heavenly title, acquiring your birthright in heaven. Perhaps as a Scion born in heaven, my father arranged for me the position of Groomer of the West Wind, and therefore through my boss I can file the paperwork to requisition miracles related to tigers, metal, the autumn, and the winds. (A little odd, but this is how I'm reading it at the moment.)<br /> <br /> The Shen motif is alchemy - distilling an elixir that stokes my internal qi into a flame I can spit (Fire), refining a pill that heals all wounds (Health), or removing all impurities from a metal to create an alloy stronger than all others (Forge) in the external sense, or performing exercises to regulate my qi and become light as a breeze and fly (Sky) or concentrate the elemental aspects within myself to breath a chilling gust that freezes a lake (Frost) in the internal. In particular I've recently been pointed to Chinese cultivation novels as a good source of ideas for the alchemical control of internal forces to create miraculous effects.<br /> <br /> But a starting Shen scion has exactly one motif through which to express their purviews - alchemy. And Tianming doesn't seem like it naturally <i>fits</i> with the concept of expressing itself through alchemy or qi cultivation - a lot of the possible marvels are very odd. Maybe I could requisition the ingredients related to my position, or express my personal power to show a mortal bureaucracy how pointless it is to act against me, but these things don't seem very... natural. Both purview and motif are reasonable expressions of Shen ideas of what divine power is, but they're disparate concepts of it that don't work together at all.<br /> <br /> What kind of Marvels are intended to be done by combining these two? As they're the absolute baseline thing that all Shen scions have, it seems like marvels are almost unusable except through the combination of their starting non-pantheon purview and their pantheon motif until they acquire other ways to express their power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24151-kingofferrets","user":"kingofferrets","date":". 02-05-2022, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24151-kingofferrets","name":"kingofferrets","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T01:25:10-08:00","id":1474068,"title":"","content":"I see it as Tianming being the divine mandate that makes the fantastical alchemy, whether external or internal, possible. If any mortal tried it, nothing would happen, even if they spent a lifetime refining the process - it would take several lifetimes for a mortal to even approach the level of control a starting Scion has. It is their divine mandate that makes all of these miracles possible. So make sure you have your paperwork in order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26101-grevnor","name":"Grevnor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T20:59:37-08:00","id":1474253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grevnor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474045-the-shen-purview-and-motif-how-do-they-work-together?p=1474068#post1474068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see it as Tianming being the divine mandate that makes the fantastical alchemy, whether external or internal, possible. If any mortal tried it, nothing would happen, even if they spent a lifetime refining the process - it would take several lifetimes for a mortal to even approach the level of control a starting Scion has. It is their divine mandate that makes all of these miracles possible. So make sure you have your paperwork in order.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you'd just think of it as &quot;the Shen purview allows basically anything that could be done with the motif, as long as you're in good standing with Heaven&quot;? That seems a little questionable.<br /> <br /> ...for that matter, the fact that it <i>doesn't</i> really well represent the ability for someone to... not be happy with Chinese Heaven, and be outcast or actively reject their position, seems odd now that I think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24151-kingofferrets","name":"kingofferrets","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T19:10:24-08:00","id":1474541,"title":"","content":"I've been struggling with this exact problem, and I've been doing some reading to try and make sense of it. Alchemy and Tianming being a bit of an ill fit makes some sense, historically speaking, as the Chinese alchemical tradition is closely tied to Taoism, while the concept of Tianming has nothing really to do with Taoism, and predates alchemical doctrine by at least several hundred years. <br /> <br /> That being said, I think the concept is still workable if you take a broad view of what alchemy means. Reading some about the doctrines of alchemy, particularly internal alchemy, and the symbolic relationships to cosmology, it seems possible to affect bureaucracies (or indeed just about anything) by describing the action in terms of distilling your subject to its essence, transmuting it, or applying some of the symbolic associations of the five elements or the hexagrams of the I Ching. It's a far cry from alchemy as proto-chemistry, but from what I'm reading, real Taoist alchemy is pretty far from chemistry too.<br /> <br /> And sure, that does mean that the Shen motif can allow almost anything, but as far as I can tell the pantheon motifs generally are meant more to flavor description than to limit the use of purviews. Compare with the Theoi motif, &quot;The most high may grant their favor to those who beseech them,&quot; which appears to plainly offer carte-blanche to do anything as long as you do it in the form of asking nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T00:33:04-08:00","id":1474789,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I can see the idea there, I think. It makes me wonder - to what all is Tianming believed to apply? Is it primarily the ordering of the world - what is valued, who is placed highly due to their divine mandate, how things should be organized - or is it broader than that? Does natural law follow from Tianming, and could be different if heaven willed it so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24151-kingofferrets","name":"kingofferrets","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T07:49:26-08:00","id":1474806,"title":"","content":"That's a good question. Going by the purview description, as well as the innate power and boons described in the book, Tianming exerts its power primarily in the social arena-- it can speed up or slow down a bureaucracy, or affect other people's views and attitudes. Which might, by itself, be adequate to circumscribe the kinds of marvels that a person could enact with Tianming, but I can see an argument for opening it up a little further. <br /> <br /> Going back to the original use of the term, which was an approximate equivalent to the European &quot;divine right of kings,&quot; the myth was that nature itself would turn against an unjust ruler who no longer has the favor of the gods, sending natural disasters and famines to show that a given king no longer has the Mandate of Heaven. So you could argue that it makes sense that Tianming could be used to bend natural law, provided it does so in the narrow circumstance of punishing abuse of power or other failures to live up to what Heaven expects of one... or, I suppose, rewarding diligence in the fulfilment of one's divine role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T08:38:14-08:00","id":1474808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1474045-the-shen-purview-and-motif-how-do-they-work-together?p=1474541#post1474541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sure, that does mean that the Shen motif can allow almost anything, but as far as I can tell the pantheon motifs generally are meant more to flavor description than to limit the use of purviews. Compare with the Theoi motif, &quot;The most high may grant their favor to those who beseech them,&quot; which appears to plainly offer carte-blanche to do anything as long as you do it in the form of asking nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the pantheon Motifs come down, in varying degrees, to &quot;This is how you do magic in this culture.&quot; Sometimes they line up with PSPs, sometimes they don't, but Storyguides shouldn't use them as a reason to limit a character's ability to perform Marvels. Shen alchemy, Orisha herbalism, and \u00c6sir runework would all, in theory, be at a disadvantage against some of the quicker verbal Motifs if that were the case, so it's better to assume that characters always have things prepared beforehand or can do them with minimum effort.<br /> <br /> So yes, they're all basically there for flavour (at the moment).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}